==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]] in the Japanese version of the game, the first stage in this map had the difficulty rating "極ムズ" (Extreme, the JP equivalent to EN's "Deadly" rating).[[File:Mapsn421 00 s ja Old.png|thumb|right|Original stage name]]
*Every stage of Invasion of Poultrio has a variant of [[Doge]]. This could allude to [https://www.theoi.com/Khthonios/Hekate.html Hecate], a Greek underworld goddess who has three forms, bodies, or heads and is associated with dogs; one of her familiars is the Trojan Queen [[wikipedia:Hecuba|Hecuba]] transformed into a black dog, which may be referenced by the [[Doge Dark]]s in the [[Feathergeddon I (Merciless)|first]] and [[Feathergeddon: Swan Song (Brutal)|fourth]] stages.
*The Japanese name of each stage, 一石三鳥, translates to "Three Birds, One Stone", which is a play on the saying "to kill two birds with one stone". The "Three Birds" is a reference to the three-headed boss.
*The English name of each stage is a portmanteau of "feather" and "armageddon", with the final stage [[Feathergeddon: Swan Song (Brutal)|Feathergeddon: Swan Song]] being a play on both a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swan_song Swan song], a performer's final act before death or retirement, and in the literal sense as the song of a swan bird, referencing the boss being an avian performer and the stage being the final battle with it.

